From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:04:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Keep the target of events that IndexedDB objects pass
 on

The events of an IndexedDB request go to its transaction and the
transaction's connection ("get the parent" of IDBRequest and
IDBTransaction). DOM's dispatch, taken literally, handles a parent
that is neither a Window nor a node by setting the target to it (step
"Otherwise: set target to parent"), so the transaction and the
connection each became the event's target in their own struct of the
path: listeners there saw event.target as the transaction or the
connection and its error, and their bubbling listeners ran as
AT_TARGET even for success events, which don't bubble. Gecko, Chromium
and WebKit keep the request as the target, and the IndexedDB WPT tests
expect it.

A parent that is neither a Window nor a node is now appended to the
event path like a Window, without a shadow-adjusted target, so the
target stays the request and the parents get the capturing and
bubbling phases. Only the IndexedDB objects have such parents.

This makes the error events that "abort a transaction" fires at the
pending requests look as the spec describes to listeners on the
transaction and the connection, which transaction-abort-request-error
checks, and fixes request_bubble-and-capture and
transaction_bubble-and-capture.

Validation: WPT IndexedDB/ (4,511 subtests), 8 processes, on top of the previous commits: host SpiderMonkey 3,287 pass (P2.1: 3,278), QuickJS 3,289 (3,281; idbfactory-origin-isolation flaked, see the previous commit); DAYU200 2 processes 3,285 (3,272). The 9 newly passing subtests, the three tests in their three globals, pass 10 of 10 on both engines. /dom/events/: 217 of 217 tests as expected. /_mozilla/IndexedDB/: 82 of 82 on the host and the board. `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings` and `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`: no warning. After the P2 review the condition is `!parent.is::<Node>()`, which includes a Window: /dom/events/ and /shadow-dom/ 600 of 600 tests as expected on host SpiderMonkey.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent found the dispatch difference, wrote the change, simplified it after the P2 review and ran the WPT runs)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
